WEBVTT

1
00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:45.210
I am so used to it.

2
00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:48.210
It just doesn't sound right. Good evening everyone.

3
00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:51.210
Hallelujah, praise the Lord.

4
00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:56.210
Thank you all for coming. I asked what everyone would like to sit in the middle section.

5
00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:59.210
That's just nice. Then we can look at everyone for a moment.

6
00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:03.210
Sorry everyone if that is uncomfortable.

7
00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:05.210
It's the weekend too.

8
00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:07.210
Hallelujah.

9
00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:10.210
Shall we pray together?

10
00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:15.210
Is it a good idea? Maybe we can stand and then we will pray for tonight.

11
00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:19.210
Hallelujah.

12
00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:26.210
Father in heaven, I am very excited about tonight and I think several people in this room are too.

13
00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:30.210
Erik is wonderful to know you.

14
00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:34.210
Erik wants to start tonight by giving you the glory and the honor for who you are.

15
00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:41.210
Not even about what you have done. You deserve all the glory and honor for who you are.

16
00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:45.210
The person God. The one who made everything.

17
00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:48.210
But even before he made everything, he was already God.

18
00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:51.210
And he already deserved all the honor and glory.

19
00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:54.210
But there was no one to give him honor and glory.

20
00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:59.210
And that is why he made a wonderful creation, so that all of creation can worship God.

21
00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:05.210
And Lord, I consider it a privilege to know you in 2025.

22
00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:09.210
It is a privilege in the world we live in that we may know you.

23
00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:12.210
It is a privilege to know the name of Jesus.

24
00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:18.210
For in the letter to the Colossians it says that Jesus is the complete picture of who God is.

25
00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:23.210
And very often I think to myself, thank you Lord that I may know Jesus.

26
00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:25.210
For in this way I may know God.

27
00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:29.210
And we may talk to Him and we may sing for Him and we may live for Him.

28
00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:32.210
Lord, I am so glad that we may know you.

29
00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:39.210
But I also feel such a privilege that we may be a church in 2025.

30
00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:42.210
In the area where we have been placed by the Father.

31
00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:46.210
That we may be a light in the society in which we live.

32
00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:52.210
It is a privilege that we may be a church in this time, in this place.

33
00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:59.210
I repeat in this prayer, it is a privilege that we may be a church in this area and in this time.

34
00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:04.210
Not in the 60s, not in the 2050s.

35
00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:07.210
Oh no, in the 2050s we will still exist, that's for sure.

36
00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:10.210
But now, at this moment we are here.

37
00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.210
And for that I want to thank you Lord.

38
00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:14.210
I want to thank you for everyone in Open Church.

39
00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:19.210
I want to thank you for the people who have been here since day 1 when Reobot was founded.

40
00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:26.210
And I also want to thank you for the person who came to visit for the first time last Sunday and who is not even sure about the gospel yet.

41
00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:32.210
Lord, I thank you for everyone in Open Church, in and around Open Church.

42
00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:34.210
We give you the glory and the honor.

43
00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:38.210
We give you the glory and the honor for what you are doing.

44
00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:42.210
We give you the glory and the honor for the past year.

45
00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:46.210
We will talk about it shortly, but we are here and we are watching it.

46
00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:49.210
We give you the glory and the honor. You are an almighty God.

47
00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:53.210
In the name of King Jesus. Hallelujah. Amen.

48
00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:57.210
Amen. Let us comfortably sit down in the name of Jesus.

49
00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:00.210
Praise God.

50
00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:08.210
I have asked Bram to do this presentation with me.

51
00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:14.210
And instead of me giving a whole story and then Bram also giving a whole story.

52
00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:17.210
And then you would be here until 12 o'clock.

53
00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:23.210
I have chosen that it is best, in consultation with Bram, that Bram will do the presentation.

54
00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:29.210
And that Bram will handle the informative side and I will handle the humorous side. Okay?

55
00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:36.210
Bram Volwassen, I am Tim. Amen.

56
00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:41.210
You are not on.

57
00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:47.210
That was my purpose. See?

58
00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:49.210
Look, all this technology is a bit difficult.

59
00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:54.210
I am just full of wow stories.

60
00:06:55.210 --> 00:07:00.210
I am so excited about what I have been able to experience with the construction team this past year.

61
00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:02.210
The things we have seen.

62
00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:04.210
From the first prayer.

63
00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:12.210
From the first revelation that came in that God said Tim it is time to start building.

64
00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:13.210
From that first moment.

65
00:07:14.210 --> 00:07:17.210
And the subsequent prayer of Lord, is this you?

66
00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:21.210
Everyone knows that feeling. Is this my thought or is this God?

67
00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:22.210
Everyone knows that thought.

68
00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:24.210
Lord, is this you?

69
00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:26.210
And that you start to pray about it.

70
00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:31.210
And from that moment a rollercoaster of confirmations, green lights, open doors.

71
00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:33.210
That is really amazing.

72
00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:36.210
And to be able to build a project together.

73
00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:45.210
And to be able to establish a project about how we can build a new building together with God.

74
00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:51.210
And I feel it, while we are working on that chronicle study.

75
00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:55.210
And I see that, I am not David, I am just Tim.

76
00:07:56.210 --> 00:07:59.210
But how the Holy Spirit gave David blueprints.

77
00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:02.210
That same God, that same clear God is still present.

78
00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:04.210
He is still alive, that God.

79
00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:06.210
And He is still clear.

80
00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:07.210
And He still gives blueprints.

81
00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:09.210
And He still gives vision.

82
00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:10.210
And He still gives plans.

83
00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:12.210
And He still provides.

84
00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:14.210
And He still gives everything.

85
00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:18.210
As we read in the Bible, that same God is still the same God.

86
00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:21.210
Yesterday, today, and forever. Amen.

87
00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:29.210
And it seemed good to us, after a year, 2024.

88
00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:31.210
And wow, we have prayed for it.

89
00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:33.210
And wow, a theme.

90
00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:35.210
And we have taught the Bible.

91
00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:38.210
And we have also shouted very loudly from the podium.

92
00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:42.210
At least, I have tried to make it as clear as possible.

93
00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:47.210
We are building a building, but that is not what it is really about.

94
00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:49.210
We are building temples of the Holy Spirit.

95
00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:53.210
All those people who come in, that is what it is really about.

96
00:08:53.210 --> 00:08:55.210
The building is absolutely secondary.

97
00:08:55.210 --> 00:08:57.210
We must never honor a building.

98
00:08:57.210 --> 00:09:00.210
It is truly about the temples of the Holy Spirit.

99
00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:06.210
But to be able to give that an accommodation, that is why God has truly given us a mission.

100
00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:07.210
Build my house.

101
00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:09.210
Now is the time to start building.

102
00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:14.210
And from the moment that started rolling out, we began to plan, we began to talk.

103
00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:20.210
And so for 2024, we have given updates about that, but it seemed to Bram and me and the board and the construction team,

104
00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:25.210
it seemed very good to us to do just that now, and you will find out about that in the presentation,

105
00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:29.210
to give an update, actually from the beginning to the end,

106
00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:33.210
of what we have experienced and where we stand now?

107
00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:34.210
What is the current status?

108
00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:37.210
Because we are actually at a milestone now.

109
00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:41.210
So Bram, over to you.

110
00:09:41.210 --> 00:09:45.210
And if I give you a shoulder, if I do this, then I also want to share something.

111
00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:49.210
We will see how that works together.

112
00:09:49.210 --> 00:09:51.210
Yes, it's a conversation, folks.

113
00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:55.210
So it's not fancy-nancy, we just talk through it all together.

114
00:09:58.210 --> 00:10:00.210
How do they say that in good Dutch?

115
00:10:00.210 --> 00:10:02.210
Fasten your seatbelt.

116
00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:04.210
We have a lot to discuss.

117
00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:15.210
And I would say, I have done my best to make it as clear as possible

118
00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:17.210
and to make it as understandable as possible.

119
00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:20.210
It's not strange at all if there is a question here or there,

120
00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:26.210
but could you please remember that question well and address it at the end,

121
00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:30.210
for otherwise other people will lose the thread of the story.

122
00:10:30.210 --> 00:10:32.210
Can we agree on that?

123
00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:34.210
Yes.

124
00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:43.210
I think there are people here who have no idea how we actually came to this building.

125
00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:47.210
So let's take a little look at history.

126
00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:54.210
And when you look back at the history of the church, you say, how good God is?

127
00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:59.210
A very, very long time ago, shortly after World War II,

128
00:10:59.210 --> 00:11:06.210
this building was originally constructed for the non-profit organization Lenteleven.

129
00:11:07.210 --> 00:11:14.210
To, as it was called then, guide low-educated girls in the things you need in life.

130
00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:18.210
But it was beautiful work. It was good work.

131
00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:25.210
And so it already had a social function in the community here from the very beginning.

132
00:11:25.210 --> 00:11:34.210
This place has had a building function, a social function in the city of Lommel all this time.

133
00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:42.210
Of course, there have been various renovations, because our front door is now a few meters forward.

134
00:11:43.210 --> 00:11:45.210
It's no longer where it used to be.

135
00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:49.210
We have also renovated a few things ourselves.

136
00:11:50.210 --> 00:12:00.210
And since the church started in 1983, well in the beginning the church was quite small of course, that has grown.

137
00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:06.210
But quite quickly there was interest in whether we could not get a permanent building.

138
00:12:06.210 --> 00:12:13.210
And for at least 15 years there have been attempts in dozens of places, am I exaggerating?

139
00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:18.210
No, dozens of places tried, is this it? Is that it? On an industrial estate.

140
00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:26.210
Another little building. Oh yes, let's try the postage stamp procedure. Article 19 procedure to change a zoning plan.

141
00:12:26.210 --> 00:12:29.210
Every time it didn't work out.

142
00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:38.210
And almost always that had something to do with the designation of each piece of land in the Netherlands and in Belgium having a certain designation.

143
00:12:39.210 --> 00:12:47.210
Until, in 2003, a phone call came in the evening to the pastors.

144
00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:53.210
There is a property for sale there. It is becoming available. Through, through, through.

145
00:12:54.210 --> 00:13:03.210
This area. This area is a blue zone in Belgium and that is therefore a public utility or a social facility or I don't know exactly what the term is.

146
00:13:03.210 --> 00:13:05.210
The designation was already good.

147
00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:19.210
Long story short. The non-profit organization that had meanwhile come to life in another organization could no longer maintain this property.

148
00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:26.210
Had to part with it. And we then received a unique agreement which is a miracle in itself.

149
00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:32.210
We were given five years to buy the property.

150
00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:36.210
At a pre-established price. In the meantime, we rented it.

151
00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:41.210
And so we could already renovate it for our own use in the meantime.

152
00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:46.210
That is a considerable investment. You only make that if you know you can use it long-term.

153
00:13:46.210 --> 00:13:52.210
And we could start organizing that we were going to buy it.

154
00:13:52.210 --> 00:13:57.210
And indeed, in 2004 the property was opened.

155
00:13:57.210 --> 00:14:01.210
If you look closely, you can really see a few familiar faces here.

156
00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:04.210
I see Pastor Kees Lauree.

157
00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:14.210
This was then the mayor of Veldhoven, the then mayor of the city of Lommel, who officially opened the property.

158
00:14:15.210 --> 00:14:26.210
And in 2009 we purchased the property, complete with over 1 hectare of land, for 425,000 euros.

159
00:14:29.210 --> 00:14:34.210
We received a mortgage from ABN AMRO for a little less.

160
00:14:34.210 --> 00:14:37.210
I don't know the amount off the top of my head.

161
00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:42.210
The church began to flourish with the new opportunities.

162
00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:45.210
Started to expand further.

163
00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:52.210
And in 2013 it really became cramped and this hall was placed.

164
00:14:52.210 --> 00:14:56.210
This hall, the rough construction was done by construction company Altes.

165
00:14:56.210 --> 00:14:58.210
Good construction company.

166
00:14:58.210 --> 00:15:02.210
And we managed the finishing ourselves at that time.

167
00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:10.210
With everything that is now here, the value of this property is 1,215,000 euros.

168
00:15:10.210 --> 00:15:13.210
Today we are going to name names and specifics.

169
00:15:13.210 --> 00:15:16.210
Today we are simply going to mention numbers.

170
00:15:16.210 --> 00:15:19.210
For costs, for financing, for whatever you can think of.

171
00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:28.210
What we have here, we take for granted in everyday life.

172
00:15:29.210 --> 00:15:32.210
But that is already a miracle in itself.

173
00:15:32.210 --> 00:15:37.210
How this has developed, how we have been able to work this out as a congregation.

174
00:15:37.210 --> 00:15:41.210
How we have seen the hand of God to function in this place.

175
00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:48.210
What are we planning then?

176
00:15:52.210 --> 00:15:54.210
Let's take a look.

177
00:15:55.210 --> 00:15:59.210
This is a drawing of the current situation.

178
00:16:01.210 --> 00:16:06.210
You see here in black this hall.

179
00:16:06.210 --> 00:16:11.210
And that little block, that striped one, those are the terraces.

180
00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:17.210
And that strange shape with all the bulges going in every direction.

181
00:16:17.210 --> 00:16:20.210
So this is the original old part of the building.

182
00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:24.210
And that old part is really old.

183
00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:27.210
Especially the foundation in it.

184
00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:31.210
It can't just keep going like this.

185
00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:35.210
Either we have to renovate it very drastically or it has to come down.

186
00:16:35.210 --> 00:16:37.210
One of the two.

187
00:16:37.210 --> 00:16:43.210
And if we renovate it, we still have something that doesn't fit the current use of the church.

188
00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:45.210
So that doesn't make much sense.

189
00:16:46.210 --> 00:16:50.210
And so a plan has been developed step by step.

190
00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:56.210
And this is essentially the summary of the plan.

191
00:16:56.210 --> 00:16:58.210
I will come back to that.

192
00:16:58.210 --> 00:17:03.210
As you all know, we have acquired two pieces of land.

193
00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:10.210
And on the left side, there will be a children's church.

194
00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:16.210
Then we see in gray the room we are currently in.

195
00:17:16.210 --> 00:17:23.210
And on the right side, that old bumpy section will disappear, and a new hall will be built.

196
00:17:24.210 --> 00:17:27.210
This hall will have two new functions.

197
00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:31.210
That half will become a small room.

198
00:17:32.210 --> 00:17:38.210
And this half will be an entrance, lounge area, etcetera.

199
00:17:39.210 --> 00:17:43.210
So that we also have space to drink coffee when there are more people.

200
00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:53.210
This is the detailed view of these sections.

201
00:17:57.210 --> 00:18:02.210
While construction is underway, the church must of course continue to function.

202
00:18:02.210 --> 00:18:04.210
So that will happen in phases.

203
00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:08.210
We have been working very hard on phase 0.

204
00:18:08.210 --> 00:18:11.210
All those drawings are the result of phase 0.

205
00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:14.210
You need to develop your plan.

206
00:18:14.210 --> 00:18:16.210
That goes together with an architect.

207
00:18:16.210 --> 00:18:18.210
You need to have the drawings for that.

208
00:18:19.210 --> 00:18:21.210
You need to have a permit.

209
00:18:21.210 --> 00:18:24.210
Apply for it and go through that whole process.

210
00:18:24.210 --> 00:18:26.210
I will come back to that in a moment.

211
00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:30.210
You need to arrange the financing.

212
00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:32.210
I also have a few words to say about that.

213
00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:38.210
There are also things like...

214
00:18:38.210 --> 00:18:42.210
To make that plan, the entire site needs to be measured.

215
00:18:42.210 --> 00:18:44.210
Let a surveyor come for a moment.

216
00:18:44.210 --> 00:18:48.210
He marks every tree on a drawing.

217
00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:50.210
Where is it? How big is it?

218
00:18:50.210 --> 00:18:52.210
Is it a conifer or a deciduous tree?

219
00:18:52.210 --> 00:18:54.210
Yes, because that matters.

220
00:18:56.210 --> 00:18:58.210
A little later, an asbestos investigation needs to be done.

221
00:18:58.210 --> 00:19:00.210
If you are going to demolish, there is asbestos in it.

222
00:19:00.210 --> 00:19:04.210
Because if there is asbestos in it, then men in white suits have to come.

223
00:19:04.210 --> 00:19:08.210
And then you pay for white suits, I should just say.

224
00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:10.210
You understand what I mean, right?

225
00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:15.210
All part of the development of your plan.

226
00:19:15.210 --> 00:19:17.210
Of course, you also talk to the construction company.

227
00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:21.210
You also discuss the initial cost estimates, etcetera.

228
00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:24.210
By the way, an interesting process.

229
00:19:27.210 --> 00:19:29.210
I think I've already told half of this.

230
00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:38.210
Because when you start developing a plan, you need to have a few starting points.

231
00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:40.210
You need to have a foundation.

232
00:19:40.210 --> 00:19:44.210
Because there is no end to ideas, there is no end to options.

233
00:19:44.210 --> 00:19:48.210
So you need to create some support for yourself.

234
00:19:48.210 --> 00:19:58.210
And we see that the church has roughly doubled in attendance since this hall was established.

235
00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:02.210
Do we want to build a church of a thousand people?

236
00:20:02.210 --> 00:20:07.210
